; Minimal Startup-Sequence for the read-only bring-up.
;
; The standard sequence is deliberately not used here.  It performs file
; management on SYS: (it makes directories, moves things, writes ENV:), and
; during bring-up the medium is mounted read-only and must stay byte-identical
; across board runs.  Anything that needs to write goes to RAM: instead, and
; content is added to this file one line at a time, each audited.
;
; Nothing below writes to SYS:.

Echo "AROS esp32p4-riscv, read-only bring-up"
Echo "SYS: is mounted read-only on purpose; transient state belongs in RAM:"
